# The reproducibility tree is a VERBATIM BYTE COPY of the research monorepo's
# src/biosqa (reproducibility/scripts/sync_from_src.py), and
# tests/test_reproducibility_sync.py compares RAW BYTES to prove it has not drifted.
#
# On Windows with core.autocrlf=true, git checks these files out with CRLF while the
# monorepo originals are LF. Byte equality is then impossible and the sync test fails
# with a full-file "drift" that is really just line endings -- which is exactly what
# happened after a merge re-materialised the tree. CI never saw it because the runners
# check out LF.
#
# Pin the checkout so the byte-copy contract can actually hold on every platform.
reproducibility/**/*.py text eol=lf

# The shipped ONNX graphs are gated by an onnx_sha256 in their model cards: any
# newline translation would change the digest and refuse to load. Never touch them.
*.onnx binary
*.png binary
